       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The dose is double the maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You also aren't a prescriber, so I can't accept your confirmation as clinical sign-off.\n\nTo move this forward, a licensed prescriber needs to enter or approve the order directly. They can choose a safe regimen, for example:\n\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- A lower starting dose with titration, such as 500 mg twice daily with meals\n\nIf the prescriber reviews the patient and still wants a dose above 2,550 mg/day, they should document that rationale and confirm the formulation with pharmacy. I can enter an order once a clinician provides the regimen and their name for the note."
